=====================

 S~S  Release notes, update to Alpha publishment candidate : app-events SimpleSal App

------------------------------------------

    SimpleSal dependency alert: the software in this App identified FIXITs in SimpleSal.

         This software requires the version of SimpleSal labeled 260327 (v0.9f).

------------------------------------------

    This publishment of software contains at least one error at runtime that results in a hard fault.

    Unless this software is configured in such a way that makes the hard fault not occur, that is.

------------------------------------------

    This publishment generates two warnings during the compilation, for variables defined but used.
    This violates the publishment principles of SimpleSal and SimpleSal Apps published by TSC LLC.
    The purpose is to allow the developer to fix a small error and see the compiler react to it.

------------------------------------------

    The term "Alpha publishment candidate" implies the consumer should expect it to work as described.
    The developer will, on the other hand, be pleasantly surprised when it does work as described.

    The developer asserts that this version of the App is working as requested by the user.

------------------------------------------

    The educational goals of SimpleSal cause a publishment that can be debugged and fixed on video.

    The "v0.9b" repo commit contained multiple errors by the App working with ssTEA Events.
    In addition, the ability to see or plot statistics from the App was not implemented.

    The v0.9b software contains what are assumed to be the common mistakes new users will make.

    The v0.9c software was modified to work, while the hard fault caused was not found and so
    the v0.9c software uses a workaround to avoid the result.  The modifications, one change at
    a time, will be a video on simplesal.substack.com, to quickly demo ssTEA development/debug tools.

------------------------------------------

    The intention is to demonstrate the hidden complexities within ssTEA that support the main
    educational goal.  Extensive explanatory messages are enabled in the failing version simply
    to show how ssTEA explanatory messages communicate the condition of the App to the developer.

    The change from nonworking to working eliminates non-App messages during initialization; then,
    the periodic display of the ssTEA statistics for each Event will show ssTEA at runtime.

------------------------------------------

